  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-\\frac{5}{2},$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{2})\\cup (-\\frac{5}{2},\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/assets/be93340e6c9bd5cad811cb5c5d879c2ad86fbf70eba1f53546a5f8b2fadbd074.png)",
